# The same kernel with a left window of 768: the key loop's lower bound
# adds a branch, block 2 grows from 55 to 63 instructions, and the block
# past line 118's branch runs when `%r68 = ⌊%r69/64⌋`, the same for the
# whole CTA, the two bounds' blocks. The trip counts stay unknown for
# the same reasons, the inner key loop's still depending on the CTA
# index through the tile loop.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/gluon/attn_fwd_ws_kernel.w768.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/gluon/attn_fwd_ws_kernel.w768.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
CHECK: /-------------  <block 1>        gluon_attn_fwd.py:79-229       93  128 in 4 warps (⌊%tid.x/32⌋ < 4)             $L__BB0_62, <block 2>
CHECK: |  |      /---  <block 2>        gluon_attn_fwd.py:98-118       63  <= 128 in <= 4 warps (⌊%tid.x/32⌋ < 4)       $L__BB0_38, $L__tmp5
